/* func_titlescreen_8007ABAC (0x8007ABAC, titlescreen overlay).
 *
 * The whole title-screen state machine: the intro cutscene timing and skip,
 * CD streaming of the title sprite sheet, the memory-card menu tree (detect /
 * select / read / format / create-save, with retry and checksum-repair paths),
 * the save-file picker, and the demo-timeout fades. Runs once per frame before
 * func_titlescreen_8007CEE4.
 *
 * Owns the overlay's rodata: the BASCUS save-file name string (0x4) and its
 * substate jump table (0x1C, jtbl_8007AA54) — both emitted by this object's
 * .rodata and slot-placed.
 *
 * STATUS: 99.7% (2140/2147 insns). The old rodata-packing blocker is SOLVED —
 * gen_slots_ld now skips the subsumed later pieces owned by a flipped function
 * (the single C .rodata blob covers the string + jtbl contiguously), so the
 * override links cleanly. Sole residue: a 7-insn register-allocation tie at the
 * func_80016698 CD-kickoff call (line ~81). The original materializes the
 * -0x40000 constant into arg reg a1 and keeps the D_800785E8 pointer in a temp
 * v0 (`addu a1,v0,a1`); our gcc allocates the pointer to a1 and the constant to
 * v0 (`addu a1,a1,v0`). Root cause: the 5th (stack) arg 600 occupies v0, is
 * stored, and v0 is recycled — the original reuses it for the LATE-loaded
 * pointer; our gcc reuses it for the const. Every source form tried (temp hoist,
 * array-index, int-cast, constant-first `-0x40000 + p`, pointer-const base,
 * variable offset, named 5th arg, precomputed a0/a3 temps, moved state store,
 * shared size var) canonicalizes to the identical output. A `register char *bp
 * asm("$2")` pin fixes the addu but forces an early pointer load -> 9 diffs (net
 * worse). Permuter: full infra built under build/perm/func_titlescreen_8007ABAC
 * (persistent-container compile/objdump shims, single-fn asm-built target.o,
 * base score 3195), ran ~39000 iterations (overnight, -j8) with ZERO sub-floor
 * results — the randomizer's transform space does not reach this v0-reuse flip.
 * Genuine permuter-or-never wall; the rest of the function is byte-identical.
 *
 * 2026-07-25-1 unattended permuter session (~15m, ~9800 iterations via the
 * standard `open-spyro permuter` path, timed out at the 15m budget): best score
 * 3195 — identical to the base score, zero sub-floor results, only 2 output
 * dirs. CORROBORATES the overnight ~39000-iteration finding above: the
 * randomizer's transform space genuinely does not reach the v0-reuse flip.
 * Treat as settled; do not spend further unattended permuter time here.
 *
 * 2026-08-21-1 — THE "EVERY SOURCE FORM CANONICALIZES" CLAIM IS RETIRED, and
 * the root cause above is wrong in a way that matters.  Do not re-run the
 * permuter here: the residue is not a scheduling tie at all.
 *
 * WHAT IT ACTUALLY IS.  The block is
 *   (set (reg P) (mem D_800785E8))      ; the pointer
 *   (set (reg C) (const_int -262144))   ; the constant
 *   (set (reg:SI 5 a1) (plus (reg P) (reg C)))
 * and `local-alloc.c block_alloc` walks the insn's operands `for (i = 1; ...)`
 * calling `combine_regs (operand_i, operand_0)` and BREAKING ON THE FIRST WIN.
 * Operand 1 is P, so P gets TIED to the destination hard reg a1 and C falls to
 * find_reg, which hands it the recycled v0 -> `addu a1,a1,v0`.  The original
 * has the tie land on operand 2 instead (`addu a1,v0,a1`).  So this is a
 * combine_regs TIE question, not a scheduler or a qty_compare question, and
 * that is why every scheduling-flavoured probe in the note above came back
 * byte-identical.  Verified with the SD-2c probe: dispositions are
 * `134 in 5` (P -> a1) and `136 in 2` (C -> v0); both are priority-1 stragglers
 * at sched1 (`cc1 -dS` prints priority = 1 for all six insns of the block, no
 * birthing boost on any of them).
 *
 * A SOURCE FORM THAT DOES FLIP IT (this is the new fact).  An A195 ref dial on
 * the constant — `int off; do { off = -0x40000; } while (0);` with the call
 * written `D_800785E8 + off` — is LENGTH-EXACT (2147) and emits
 * **`addu a1,v0,a1`, exactly the original**.  It is the only form found that
 * moves this insn at all.
 * WHY IT IS NOT A MATCH YET: the do/while is also an A200 cse barrier, and the
 * barrier lets cse merge D_80076B90 with the symbol 40 bytes below it into one
 * held base, so `lui v0/addiu v0/lw v0,0(v0)` at orig 117-119 becomes
 * `lui s3/addiu s3/lw v0,0(s3)` and the a0 load at the call site becomes
 * `lw a0,-40(s3)`.  That saves an insn there and the saving is spent
 * reshuffling the call-site block.  Net 14 aligned vs the baseline 6.
 * The open question is therefore narrow and named: **raise the constant's
 * reg_n_refs without ending cse's ebb.**  flow.c's `loop_depth` weighting is
 * the only mechanism that raises reg_n_refs, which is why every non-loop
 * spelling is inert.
 *
 * MEASURED THIS SESSION (aligned score; baseline 6 over 3 regions — note the
 * LINKED count is 7, use the content-aligned one to drive this park):
 *   6   baseline; a plain `int off = -0x40000;` named temp (inert, as the
 *       note above says); `n = 600` named 5th arg; `n` shared with the
 *       adjacent `D_80078D78.unk_0x10 = 1;` store (the constant store is
 *       rematerialised by reload per A220, so the second set is deleted and
 *       reg_n_sets never rises — the same F14i trap as level_27's `rx`).
 *   14  the A195 dial at the call site (addu CORRECT, cse barrier costs more).
 *   16  a shared `vram` pointer local across the two arms.
 *   18/25  the dial hoisted above the CD poll / to the top of the case — both
 *       come out SHORT (2145 / 2142) and will not link.
 * Also measured: making the pointer multi-block does NOT reach the call site —
 * gcc keeps a fresh block-local pseudo there because the load carries a
 * REG_EQUIV, so `reg_qty < 0` never holds for the operand that matters.
 */

